{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1384306-ideas-for-vampire-characters","id":1384306,"title":"Ideas for Vampire characters? +","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-04-27T17:31:07-07:00","id":1384306,"title":"Ideas for Vampire characters? +","content":"I miss the old Clan books, mainly because I used to really enjoy reading through some of the, often very original pregenerated characters that used to be included in the back. So, on that basis, can anybody present their original ideas for characters, possibly with stats (in any edition).<br /> <br /> Just to quickly get going, I\u2019d like to cite a short movie, called The Voorman Problem as an inspiration for a Malkavian vampire: <br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=EaB2wiiOgHM\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=EaB2wiiOgHM\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=EaB2wiiOgHM\" target=\"_blank\"> https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=EaB2wiiOgHM </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> That is, the character believes himself to be a God, that created the universe and everything in it (including you and all your memories) as a toy to play with, about seven days ago. In the context of vampire, (s)he would be able to use a high level of Dominate to be able to persuade and undermine everything other people assumes in the world today as being wrong. Like for example, Belgium doesn\u2019t exist. Cloud Memory, Dementation (obviously) and The Forgetful Mind would be the basis of the Disciplines, possibly at the expense of everything else. The type of predator could be a Consensualist, persuading victims, but what I think would be more fun is that the character is a Scene Queen - with the scene being psychiatric treatment. The character would actively seek out psychological assessment and treatment and, after the interviewing psychiatrist mentally begins to collapse, works it into the interview process to be able to \u2018sample' the blood in some sort of religious or scientific experiment. As the reputation of the patient begins to attract more pychiatric assessment, the vampire might start to enthrall them into doing extra work too. Social and Mental Stats high, especially Manipulation and Intelligence, and Physical stats low. <br /> <br /> I may type out the details later on, if people have updated their own ideas first.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2517-trippy","name":"Trippy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2517_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1018"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-27T18:47:29-07:00","id":1384329,"title":"","content":"Hey. I could add a character for an V5 Ancilla game I made tonight. Maybe you'll like it: <span style=\"color:#454545\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:17px\"><br /> <b>Vampire V5</b></span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#454545\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>Character: Victoria \u00bbVi\u00ab Herschel</b></span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#454545\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Core Concept: Whorehouse Jewel</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#454545\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Name: <b>Vivian Hawthorne</b></span></span></span><ul><li>Born in 1850 as the twelfth child of <b>Sir John Herschel</b>, the astronomer and his cousin <b>Margaret Brodie Stewart</b>, Victoria was thought to be the last child of the family, her mother being 40 years old and it had been four years since she had last conceived.</li> <li>The long line of scientists, astronomers, and inventors was not restricted to the male side of the family, although the girls were expected to learn only to entertain themselves and their future spouses.</li> <li>She grew up with her father a stranger, as distant in his love and recognition as the spheres and moons he had chosen to spend his time with.</li> </ul><br /> <span style=\"color:#454545\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Background:</span></span></span><ul><li>Victoria had eleven older siblings, her oldest sister having married a prime minister\u2019s son when the little blond angel was only two, her one younger sister <b>Constance Ann</b> was born when Victoria was five.</li> <li>The house was full of literature, charts, trinkets from South Africa, private tutors and staff, taking care of all needs as they appeared with a strict distance that never provided a loving home.</li> <li>Her official introduction into the gentle society was barely a splash as neither <b>Julia Edith</b>, <b>Matilda</b> nor <b>Francisca</b> had been married yet and it would be years before Sir John Herschel would give his daughter away.</li> <li>Victoria was a rebelious child, never accepting authority and the relentless strive her father and brothers had for the ephemeral stars, fighting against the societal shackles that bound her siblings into the same kind of loveless relationship her parents had while envying the common peasants for the freedom to see and experience the physical world before them.</li> <li>When <b>Mr. O\u2019Toole</b>, a man she had inexplicably felt drawn to, took her to an opium den, he took her virginity and had he not embraced her right then and there, she would have bleed out.</li> </ul><br /> <span style=\"color:#454545\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Embrace:</span></span></span><ul><li><b>Craigh O\u2019Toole</b> was still a Neonate and grandchilde of an elder of the learned clan who was only ever refered to as the <b>Skullsplitter</b>, a warrior of nordic decent who had called northern Ireland his home for the better part of half a millenium.</li> <li>Craigh\u2019s Sire was less then pleased by the transgression but had an uncanny way with words, making many people outright forget Victoria Herschel\u2019s existence, including her parents and siblings, but also potential suitors, servants and staff.</li> <li>It was quite an undertaking, costing her dearly and for the transgression she and her Sire were banned to the new world.</li> </ul><br /> <span style=\"color:#454545\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Unlife:</span></span></span><ul><li>Victoria has spent close to 150 years in various cities around the country, most of the time blood bound to Mr. O\u2019Toole, he himself being a toy to various elders of the clan.</li> <li>She created a Childe herself back in the 1970s, a truck driver by the name of <b>Joseph Clover</b>, who is still in her employ and close to her heart though she sometimes wonders whether his embrace was her own choice.</li> <li>For one thing it gave her a sense of being part of the age of aquarius, a renewed love for the celestial bodies of her childhood and the occult world she found herself in, as well as keeping her in touch with modern times.</li> <li>Nowadays she owns a roadside whorehouse on the outskirts of the city, run by her ghoul <b>Rosie</b> and mostly frequented by truck drivers and whoever Victoria chooses to summon.</li> <li>She has taken them name Vivian and is working as one of the girls herself, the prized piece of ass, feeding in the process and leaving the men and women wanting for more paying with coin, boon, and information to have her drink their blood.</li> <li>There are about a dozen other girls working the premises and Joe and his boys try to make sure they notice anyone being smuggled into the city, bringing them to Rosie\u2019s.</li> </ul><br /> <span style=\"color:#454545\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Clan: <b>Brujah</b></span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#454545\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Sire: <b>Craigh O\u2019Toole</b></span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#454545\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Generation: <b>11th</b></span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#454545\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Blood Potency: <b>2</b></span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#454545\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>Attributes:</b></span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#454545\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Strength: 3 | Charisma: 4 | Intelligence: 2<br /> Dexterity: 2 | Manipulation: 3 | Wits: 3</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#454545\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Stamina: 1 | Composure: 2 | Resolve: 2</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#454545\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Health: 4 | Willpower: 4 | Humanity: 6</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#454545\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Blood Potency: 2</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#454545\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>Skills:</b></span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#454545\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Victoria learned the trade first by her Sire, then during many years feeding on street urchins turning tricks and hookers selling themselves in port towns along the east coast. <b>Persuasion 3 (Seduction)</b></span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#454545\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">She had to understand what people want, what they care for, what they would do to get what they crave and after a century she reads people like open books. <b>Insight 3 (Desires)</b><br /> In many professions such as this, truth and honesty are not tools of the trade but rather pitfalls to avoid when trying to get by night after night. Victoria had to lie about her origin, her state and sometimes her Sire and Clan to survive to the modern day. <b>Subterfuge 2</b></span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#454545\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">When you work in a whorehouse you inevitably deal with the societal underbelly of the city, dealing with hudlums, gangsters, smugglers, dealers, politicians and the eventual murderer. <b>Streetwise 2</b></span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#454545\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Back in her childhood days, though she was in a constant state of rebellion against her distant father, Victoria picked up a lot of knowledge about the stars, trajectories, gravity and the high heavens which she infrequently updates through books and online papers. <b>Science 3 (Astronomy)</b></span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#454545\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Victoria began her unlife as a lover, not a fighter and to this day she has found it far more fortuitous to scare someone straight then to deal with traumata, bloodstains and a corpse. <b>Intimidation 2</b></span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#454545\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">She remembers how to behave properly in a high society setting and though it might seems extraordinarily classic by now, older Kindred will most certainly respect her efforts if not her manners. <b>Etiquette 1</b></span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#454545\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">It goes without saying that she does have the occasional public figure visiting her premises and spends a night or two a month entertaining local politicians, lobbyists or staff members, gradually accumulating a pool of political knowledge and secrets. <b>Politics 1</b></span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#454545\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">The same is true of wealthy patrons and men and women working for them, doing her taxes for her, giving her advice on spending and saving, wanting to please for that sweet, sweet Kiss. <b>Finance 1</b></span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#454545\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Unlife is not as peaceful as anyone would hope and Victoria has had to learn how to fend for herself. She is scrawny but muscular and she packs a punch but tends to fight dirty when she has the chance. <b>Brawl 2</b></span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#454545\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">For more than a year now Joe has taught her how to fight with the heavy fire axe he sprayed matte black, a weapon he himself carries with him and Victoria having a second one just like it hanging over the mantlepiece. <b>Melee 2</b></span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#454545\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Joe also taught her the basics of driving, a skill that had eluded her until the turn of this century and one she thought she would never learn. It still is hard for her to grasp the concept of rude drivers without following her great grandsire and splitting some skulls. <b>Drive 1</b></span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#454545\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Victoria learned how to pick a lock and hotwire a car in case of an emergency that hopefully never arrives. <b>Larceny 1</b></span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#454545\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">The hardest lesson she had to learn if you ask her, would be how not to be seen or heard, something that goes directly against who she deems herself to be. She still is not very good at it. <b>Stealth 1</b></span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#454545\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Victoria really tries to stick with the times though, proving that not everyone embraced around the time of the civil war is a relic. She works her phone, orders stuff online and knows how to download new science papers whenever she feels like it. <b>Technology 1</b></span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#454545\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Languages:</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#454545\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Victoria Herschel was born into the gentle society of england and spent her living days in Kent and London. While some of her older siblings spoke Dutch as well, due to being born in South Africa, she never picked up on their secret code. <b>English</b></span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#454545\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Only after her embrace, spending decades with O\u2019Toole did she pick up on his native tongue and is fluent in Gailge by now, though hardly anyone ever speaks it around her anymore. <b>Gailge</b></span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#454545\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Ambition:</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#454545\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>\u00bbI want to have the world remember my mortal existance.\u00ab</b></span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#454545\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Desire:</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#454545\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>\u00bbI want to have Rosie\u2019s made an Elysium.\u00ab</b></span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#454545\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Convictions:</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#454545\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>\u00bbNever again let harm come to my family.\u00ab</b></span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#454545\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Touchstones:</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#454545\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>Rosie O\u2019Bannon</b>, Victoria\u2019s ghoul and madame of the house. She is a woman stuck in her middle years since the 1990s and swears on her eventual gravestone that she knew Charles Manson before he got famous. Victoria saw the rebelious fighting spirit and Rosie\u2019s blood called out to her. After a malicious run-in with a John, Victoria ghouled her, corrupting the spirit to conform to her needs. Rosie feels responsible now and takes care of the girls and regular business. Every time she tries to run away, she finds herself returning a day or two later, her will to live slowly eroding in this lusty cage.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#454545\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Predator Type: <b>Siren</b></span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#454545\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Disciplines:</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#454545\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Force of Personality 4: <b>Awe</b>, <b>Daunt</b>, <b>Lingering Kiss</b>, <b>Summon</b></span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#454545\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Force of Blood 1: <b>Lethal Body</b></span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#454545\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Flaws &amp; Advantages:</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#454545\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Family is one of the most important things for Victoria and she has always believed blood to be thicker than water, which makes her so much more susceptible to the Blood Bond. <b>Flaw: Bonding 1 (Blood Junkie)</b></span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#454545\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Not only that, family is for life. Maybe it was her lack of a loving home, maybe it was the eradication of her existence in the memories of her loved ones, but Victoria\u2019s vitae yearns to belong for eternity. <b>Flaw: Bonding 1 (Long Bond)</b></span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#454545\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">O\u2019Toole taught her to never drink on the free men and women of Ireland and he made her believe this to be her own idea and decision. Of that he is not even sure himself though, it all originating down the line perhaps. <b>Flaw: Feeding 1 (Prey Exclusion: Irish)</b></span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#454545\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Victoria\u2019s kiss is one for the ages. Her bite is highly addictive and she spreads this bloody high freely, often forgetting that she has done so and losing interest in her plaything after a short while, leaving longing Johns and Janes as husks in her wake. <b>Flaw: Retainer 1 (Stalkers)</b></span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#454545\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Sometimes she is so caught up in her lovemaking and blood drinking, she does not realize who she fucks over. Sometimes they are of strong will and resist the lingering kiss long enough to come searching for revenge instead of redemption. One such man is <b>Pavel \u00bbEvil Eye\u00ab Miroslavic</b>, a ghoul of a local Tremere who has already burned down Victoria\u2019s last haven and waits for his opportunity to see her burn. <b>Flaw: Enemy 1</b></span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#454545\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">She goes by the name of Vivian Hawthorne now, a fake I.D. she aquired with the help of one of her more talented patrons. He made sure there was enough data in the system to back it up but once his task was complete he vanished into the maw that is the masquerade. <b>Mask 1</b></span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#454545\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Victoria is a beautiful young woman, pale and slender as a bone, luring Johns and Janes to her establishment and into her bed, to drink from them and have them pay for the priviledge. <b>Looks 2 (Beautiful)</b></span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#454545\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">She feeds on her patrons, she feeds on the other girls, sometimes she consumes so much blood in a night, she is not the only one to look like a corpse, but her addictive kiss makes them come back until they die. <b>Herd 4</b></span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#454545\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Victoria is accepted throughout the city, she and her whorehouse have been fixtures of the local Kindred scene for more than two decades now and she can put you in contact with almost everyone worth talking to. <b>Status 2</b></span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#454545\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Only rarely does she take money for her services to her peers. Usually she is paid in blood and boons. Secrets will get you far as well, as long they either lead to blood or boons. Almost all of her cash is used for upkeep of the premises and girls. <b>Resources 1</b></span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#454545\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Rosie used to be someone she could identify with, but their relationship has turned steadily since Victoria is giving blood to her former friend and longtime business partner who has, in all honesty, become a servant. The madame is charming, tough and the honeypot who seems to be in charge. <b>Retainer 2</b></span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#454545\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Victoria spends her days in the basement under Rosie\u2019s place on the outskirts of town. She knows it\u2019s not the safest bet, but her last Haven was burned down half a year ago, and for now it will do to keep her cards close to her chest. <b>Haven 2, Merit 1 (Watchmen), Merit 1 (Luxury)</b></span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#454545\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Weapons:</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#454545\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Victoria does not keep weapons on her, they would ruin her flow. There are however two unregistered 9mm guns hidden in Rosie\u2019s Place, only she can never remember where exactly. The one weapon she actually trained with is the matte black fire axe Joe has gifted to her and now hangs over the mantlepiece in the lounge as an implied thread to all who dare cause trouble.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#454545\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>Heavy Melee + 3 Damage</b></span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#454545\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Experience Points:</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#454545\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>0 left, 35 spent</b></span></span></span><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25558-pangur-b\u00e1n","name":"Pangur B\u00e1n","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25558_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"23"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-27T19:56:28-07:00","id":1384341,"title":"","content":"Woah! That\u2019s an effort to get us going! Good stuff. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2517-trippy","name":"Trippy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2517_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1018"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-29T10:06:03-07:00","id":1384661,"title":"","content":"I can recommend most of the characters for the V5 starter Pack New Blood. I think most of them are really great.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26030-mfalkenb","name":"mfalkenb","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"49"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-29T15:04:30-07:00","id":1384715,"title":"","content":"A couple of dozen full character write-ups from my chronicle: <a href=\"https://www.evernote.com/shard/s666/sh/f77aa63f-2074-44b4-8b28-4bff4eb356ac/49f9d25257f004b88fd0e2d00603d94a\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.evernote.com/shard/s666/...d0e2d00603d94a</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2198-malkavian87","name":"Malkavian87","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2198_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"325"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-29T17:08:26-07:00","id":1384738,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>mfalkenb</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1384306-ideas-for-vampire-characters?p=1384661#post1384661\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I can recommend most of the characters for the V5 starter Pack New Blood. I think most of them are really great.</div> </div> </div> </div>I liked them too, although something I have as a minor observation really (as opposed to a criticism, per se) is that most of the pregens in V5 so far have been specifically designed to be integrated into the stories being told. The backstories are meshed with the scenarios, and that is cool but I sometimes feel they might not work in a more generic sense. Also, I really think all pregens should include a picture of the character wherever possible - a picture speaks a thousand words, etc.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2517-trippy","name":"Trippy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2517_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1018"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-29T18:26:25-07:00","id":1384751,"title":"","content":"The pre-gen characters in the back of the original Brujah clanbook were what originally drew me to the game back in '92. I used to have entire spiral notebooks full of nothing but premade characters for Vampire and the other games. I guess I'll have to try to find them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-29T22:54:02-07:00","id":1384783,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1384306-ideas-for-vampire-characters?p=1384751#post1384751\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The pre-gen characters in the back of the original Brujah clanbook were what originally drew me to the game back in '92. I used to have entire spiral notebooks full of nothing but premade characters for Vampire and the other games. I guess I'll have to try to find them.</div> </div> </div> </div>I\u2019 used to do similar things myself, and you can still reference the old Clan books for character ideas. It would be nice, however, to have a big directory of characters for the current edition.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2517-trippy","name":"Trippy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2517_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1018"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-30T00:02:13-07:00","id":1384792,"title":"","content":"Another option is for you to go to campaign journal sites like Obsidian Portal and look at the Vampire games there. They often provide NPC characters and PCs. Sometimes it is just a name and brief description. But some campaigns have extensive backgrounds and even mechanics.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-30T00:17:47-07:00","id":1384794,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Trippy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1384306-ideas-for-vampire-characters?p=1384783#post1384783\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I\u2019 used to do similar things myself, and you can still reference the old Clan books for character ideas. It would be nice, however, to have a big directory of characters for the current edition.</div> </div> </div> </div>A fun tool I realized during the Revised era was that if you are a Storyteller and need a coterie really quickly, just pick three or four of the premade character templates that seem to fit together. Say for example, the Tremere club owner, the Brujah DJ, and the Ventrue blood epicurean (I'm blanking on their specific titles ATM and don't have the books handy) all run a night club together. It works for Werewolf, Mage, and Dark Ages too.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-30T07:04:07-07:00","id":1384835,"title":"","content":"Andy<br /> Brujah. <br /> Concept: You were a fitness junkie, maybe you were in the forces. You lost both legs in an accident, and you were determined that it wouldn't be the end of you. You've honed your upper body to the apex. You became a paralympic contender and have always strove for greatness. So much so that your passion and drive attracted the embrace. With the power of potence, your physicality has reached the point where you're more mobile out of a wheelchair than an average person; Able to sprint and leap with just your arms to the point of masquerade breach, leading you to be dependent on a retainer to take you around in public, kept to a wheel chair. This is greatly depressing for you, but your greatest fear is that someday, you'll frenzy, and you'll leap off that chair and kill your beloved assistant. It's hard to move a body quietly with just two limbs. You feed primarily from animals and the sleeping, for although you long to hunt in other ways, you're just too memorable to try.<br /> Rollplaying hints: You're somewhere between a drill sergeant and a motivational speaker; constantly ready to inspire your coterie.<br /> <br /> Teddy<br /> Tremere<br /> A poor black male with no access to education; Your teen self was enraptured in the gangsta life, and then you went to prison for what you later realized was a series of stupid things. you were intellegent. As the years went on in prison, you eventually wanted to better yourself. Finances, history, sociology; You were going to be the first man from your neighbourhood to come out of prison in a better state than you went in. You were going to get good with money and rise to the top, and you had plenty of time to study. You enjoyed studying and spent all your time in the prison's library, going on to tutor other inmates, of all kinds, in your fields. You became a model prisoner, and you attracted the attention of the Tremere. After an arrangement, you left the prison ghouled, eager to put your financial theories to the test in the real world. After proving yourself so useful in finances and streetwise, you earned the embrace. Hermetic theory has become like a religion to you; You're like a born again christian toiling in the libraries of the chantry. It doesn't matter if the clan's oppressive; you've spent your life in prison, and the condition of the chantry is certainly better, especially as you're the main breadwinner. <br /> Rollplaying notes: you're used to dealing with unreasonable people and try to avoid offence; You try to come off as friendly unless it's clear someone's looking for problems, then it's time for an ass whooping. You believe all problems can be solved with education. <br /> <br /> The Crusading cape. <br /> Malkavian. <br /> You were a body builder, definetly; your parents were gunned down by poor people before your very eyes, maybe; You were old money rich, very questionable. That were far too invested in comic books; Certain. What the truth is and what is the lie you've constructed is makes no matter. You are who you are right now. You have an absurd amount of money, great connections, and a fantastic relationship with the city's Elders who find your antics entertaining and your politics in line with their own; you largely have a free pass on what others would consider 'poaching' so long as you don't hurt anyone personally close to anyone. You have a burning, sadistic relationship with the impoverished denizens of your city. You don't kill, you maim and rape, and you've got a lot of friends in the businesses that benefit from the violence you dish out. You dress up in a super &quot;hero&quot; costume in order to fight the dregs of society and your profeciency with obfuscate allows you to largely get away with it, you've ghouled a minor to fight with you and you've infected madness into a few opponents in the hopes of getting a longstanding rogues gallery. <br /> Rollplaying notes: You don't consciously use any of your disciplines, they just augment what you think are mundane actions. You are completely enraptured with your sick delusion and your personal goals are only to perpetuate it. You will do whatever the prince or primogen asks as he has taken up a special roll in your fantasy. You don't try to get anyone in debt with prestation; you just do what is right according to your sick sense of justice and assume that they'll just keep trouble away from you behind the scenes or that maybe you'll use them as a contact at some point. If someone gets you to break character, you'll frenzy, and it's well known at court what kind of requests will and won't work from you. They also know you'll clean up someone in their yard without compensation, so long as they word their request the right way. <br /> <i>. If possible, ask your storyteller to allow you Flight 1 or 2 (For use with a gliding cape) </i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-30T14:27:42-07:00","id":1384922,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1384306-ideas-for-vampire-characters?p=1384794#post1384794\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A fun tool I realized during the Revised era was that if you are a Storyteller and need a coterie really quickly, just pick three or four of the premade character templates that seem to fit together. Say for example, the Tremere club owner, the Brujah DJ, and the Ventrue blood epicurean (I'm blanking on their specific titles ATM and don't have the books handy) all run a night club together. It works for Werewolf, Mage, and Dark Ages too.</div> </div> </div> </div>I knew a lot of STs that did that too. And when I was first starting to play the game, it was not unusual for a new player interested in the game to arrive, and the ST would give them several options from the templates as a starting character option for their first PC. That way they could immediately start playing the game without needing to do character creation, and it'd be easy for the other players to help her on what to roll, what each power meant, etc.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-30T15:09:03-07:00","id":1384931,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1384306-ideas-for-vampire-characters?p=1384794#post1384794\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> A fun tool I realized during the Revised era was that if you are a Storyteller and need a coterie really quickly, just pick three or four of the premade character templates that seem to fit together. Say for example, the Tremere club owner, the Brujah DJ, and the Ventrue blood epicurean (I'm blanking on their specific titles ATM and don't have the books handy) all run a night club together. It works for Werewolf, Mage, and Dark Ages too.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is a fun tool to use, and illustrates why having a bank of pregenerated characters is really useful in the game. I also felt it was useful having all those illustrated characters in Clanbooks because it gave an impression of how varied and diverse the society of vampires was, and brought the WoD \u2018alive\u2019 in a sense.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2517-trippy","name":"Trippy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2517_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1018"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-30T15:11:48-07:00","id":1384932,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1384306-ideas-for-vampire-characters?p=1384835#post1384835\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Teddy<br /> Tremere<br /> A poor black male with no access to education; Your teen self was enraptured in the gangsta life, and then you went to prison for what you later realized was a series of stupid things. you were intellegent. As the years went on in prison, you eventually wanted to better yourself. Finances, history, sociology; You were going to be the first man from your neighbourhood to come out of prison in a better state than you went in. You were going to get good with money and rise to the top, and you had plenty of time to study. You enjoyed studying and spent all your time in the prison's library, going on to tutor other inmates, of all kinds, in your fields. You became a model prisoner, and you attracted the attention of the Tremere. After an arrangement, you left the prison ghouled, eager to put your financial theories to the test in the real world. After proving yourself so useful in finances and streetwise, you earned the embrace. Hermetic theory has become like a religion to you; You're like a born again christian toiling in the libraries of the chantry. It doesn't matter if the clan's oppressive; you've spent your life in prison, and the condition of the chantry is certainly better, especially as you're the main breadwinner.<br /> Rollplaying notes: you're used to dealing with unreasonable people and try to avoid offence; You try to come off as friendly unless it's clear someone's looking for problems, then it's time for an ass whooping. You believe all problems can be solved with education.</div> </div> </div> </div>That\u2019s a pretty good concept right there. Its actually got me thinking about running a Vampire game in a prison at the moment. The Voorman character above was also a prisoner at the start too. I did visit Alcatraz a few years ago, and so picked up a load of touristy things about famous prisoners, etc. It may serve as good inspiration.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2517-trippy","name":"Trippy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2517_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1018"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-30T15:18:11-07:00","id":1384935,"title":"","content":"I often wondered if Alcatraz would be a good communal haven for the Sabbat in the WoD. never was sure if in the WoD there would still be tourists that travel their or not. Part of me thinks it is a great haunt though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11720-redwulfe","name":"Redwulfe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11720_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"570"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-30T15:48:22-07:00","id":1384945,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Redwulfe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1384306-ideas-for-vampire-characters?p=1384935#post1384935\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I often wondered if Alcatraz would be a good communal haven for the Sabbat in the WoD. never was sure if in the WoD there would still be tourists that travel their or not. Part of me thinks it is a great haunt though.</div> </div> </div> </div>Didn\u2019t they have some sort of hippy commune there at some point after being shut down? I mean, we could link in some real world folklore about the place.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2517-trippy","name":"Trippy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2517_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1018"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-30T16:09:58-07:00","id":1384949,"title":"","content":"Not sure, I have never been there so my knowledge is based on the movie &quot;The Rock.&quot; and gamer brain. but that would be kinda cool to take a place like Alcatraz and look at its history and ask the question what would this place be in the world of darkness.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11720-redwulfe","name":"Redwulfe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11720_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"570"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-30T16:55:22-07:00","id":1384959,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Redwulfe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1384306-ideas-for-vampire-characters?p=1384935#post1384935\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I often wondered if Alcatraz would be a good communal haven for the Sabbat in the WoD. never was sure if in the WoD there would still be tourists that travel their or not. Part of me thinks it is a great haunt though.</div> </div> </div> </div>The entire island is a national park and part of the national historical register, so it is subject to constant patrols by the United States Park Police, who are armed federal agents. A year after it was closed in 1963, Native American activists briefly occupied the island, but in 1969, a group called United Indians of All Tribes staged a two year occupation. Today, it's frequently used by the International Indian Treaty Council for religious and cultural ceremonies. It's also hosted a number of art exhibits, usually themed around human rights and political prisoners. So, there's probably too much attention by both human authorities and various Native American supernaturals (including werebeasts, shamans, and witch hunters) for it to be a Haven. It might serve as an Elysium for the Bay Area's vampires, maybe. In my head cannon, it is the primary Hierarchy citadel fortress in the Bay Area Shadow Lands.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-30T16:57:53-07:00","id":1384961,"title":"","content":"I took some photos I took of Alcatraz, while I did my tourist thing - unfortunately they don\u2019t seem to upload here. I think the commune was Native American - there is some graffiti left from the time they were staying there (late 60s/Early 70s?) which seems to imply it. There are some interesting historical inmates that could be vampires there still - Al Capone, the \u2018Bird Man\u2019, Whitey Bulger - too.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2517-trippy","name":"Trippy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2517_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1018"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-30T17:59:33-07:00","id":1384966,"title":"","content":"It has fallen in the forum listings, but there is already an excellent thread for character ideas. As of this post, we reached 246 ideas. Some were short little vignettes, some read like full-fledged fiction.<br /> <br /> Give it a <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/860617-1001-interesting-character-ideas/page16\">look</a>.<br /> <br /> I also gave it a thread necromancy bump.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11558,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11558-nosimplehiway","user":"Nosimplehiway","date":". 04-30-2020, 09:02 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11558-nosimplehiway","name":"Nosimplehiway","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avat